{"kind":"request","text":"DD-1 build: one descriptor digest for each act (decision 17e10e32, rulings 423764c4 and bc3a5516). This request takes the build; it replaces request 4fce0637, whose conditions still name one digest for a scope.\n\n- `actDescriptorDigest(definition, kind)` under the tag `artroom-act-descriptor-1` in `domains.ts`. It covers the act's own content from section 10 of the act environment note, from the definition bytes: the act, the item types it names directly, its rules, its capabilities, and the profile only when it has a rule. No version text, name, path, other act, or runtime list. It does not follow `refs` or `values`.\n- A draft row and a retained authorization each hold the digest of their own act. `ClientOptions.descriptor` goes; the instance looks the digest up by kind.\n- One kind per authorization key: a version of another kind stops with `version`.\n- Test A: a version-only release keeps every act's digest, through the loader the instance uses. Test B: one change each to an act, a rule, an item type and the profile changes exactly the acts that share it. A change to a type reached only through refs changes none.\n- The C4 note says what an outside adopter's retained authorization does at its next version, and that the digest does not follow refs or values.\n\nDone when one gate passes on the head and the checker approves.","body":{"conditions":"per-act digest per section 10 and rulings 423764c4, bc3a5516; tests A and B; one kind per key; one gate; checker approval","target_head":"06afc9d610d3255cafd0eb9aa8f133cd5a06ae89","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}